== Example Text ==
'''Article 1 of the [[Declaration of Universal Rights]]'''

<blockquote>''Omni hom-us waa xor dhal-an, oo dign-itas iyo xuquuq-ba waa sim-an. Waxaa la siiy-ay rati-o iyo damiir, waana inay ku dhaqm-aan midk-ood walaal-nimo.''</blockquote>

'''Literal Translation:'''
<blockquote>All man-subj [verb focus] free born-are, and dignity and rights-emph [verb focus] equal-are. [Focus] to given-past reason and conscience, and-must they with act-pres each-other brother-hood.</blockquote>

'''Translation:'''
<blockquote>All sentient beings are born free and equal in dignity and rights. They are endowed with reason and conscience and should act towards one another in a spirit of brotherhood.</blockquote>

== Guide for Mercian Speakers ==
For speakers of [[Mercian]], Burawi phonology presents unique challenges, particularly with throat sounds and ejectives.

=== Pronunciation ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Letter !! Mercian Approximation !! Notes
|-
| '''X (x)''' || "H" in "Huge" (deep) || A rasping sound deep in the throat (like Scottish "Loch").
|-
| '''C (c)''' || -- || A constricted throat sound (no Mercian equivalent). Try to say "ah" while choking slightly.
|-
| '''Q (q)''' || "K" (back) || Like 'K', but produced further back in the throat.
|-
| '''Dh (dh)''' || "D" (curled) || Pronounce 'D' with the tongue curled back.
|-
| '''R (r)''' || Rolled 'R' || Trilled, as in [[Volisanian language|Volisanian]].
|-
| '''A/E/I/O/U''' || Ah, Eh, Ee, Oh, Oo || Pure vowels, never diphthongized.
|}

